Changes made:

* Now we assign QUERIES to splits instead of just slicing rows:
1. aggregate to one row per query_id, with its bought count as stratum (0-4)
2. shuffle once with seed so we get random query_id's from each bucket
3. do the 80/10/10 train/val/test split for each stratum => bought rate stays even without cutting queries


